From d18efce7ed6637388eda7c0493a95690a9c5a121 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 11:05:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] update pause: a carried turn the exit did not
 interrupt takes its stamp back; one USER_STOP_AT_EXIT spelling

Follow-up to PR #2064 review 5889131563 (t_01a1d4568dd55405), card t_01a1d45a5a226f4e.

1) pause_stands: `cut_short_by_exit` now also requires the turn result to be `interrupted`. A carried
   notification turn that completed normally just after `_exit_keeps_turn_marker` was set (before the
   exit's interrupt landed) ran to completion, so it takes the write-ahead `carried_turn_paused` stamp
   back and the continuation no longer names it (CARRIED_TURN_NOTE).
2) prompt_turn reads the exit's user-Stop flag through `exit_job_receipts.USER_STOP_AT_EXIT`, the same
   constant pause_stands uses, instead of the literal '_user_stop_at_exit'.
3) test_a_carried_turn_that_raises_after_its_hook_paid_keeps_naming_it is labelled a regression pin
   (green before #2064 too).

Proof: new test_a_carried_turn_that_completes_normally_while_the_backend_exits_takes_the_stamp_back
RED before the fix (`carried_turn_paused` stayed True), GREEN after. All 120 test files importing
update_pause/prompt_turn/exit_job_receipts pass on worker-3 except 2 in
tests/gateway/test_kanban_restart_continuation.py, which fail on the worker host's inventory isolation
guard ("pytest must not register boards in the real account worker inventory"), unrelated to this diff.
